ion/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f2ab3104-7e40-5b36-8b8a-4688c13efdc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-118174" :question/problem "![](images/f9/f93eab26860fffd262ce4db8927c56d77ad7710b4b7da61e190126596e968d71.png)\n\nIn the quadrilateral $ABCD$ above, determine the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "A quadrilateral has $n=4$ sides. Therefore, the sum of the interior angles of a quadrilateral must be \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2) & ={180}^{∘}\\cdot (4-2) \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding up the internal angles and solving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A+m∠B+m∠C+m∠D & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ (x+{90}^{∘})+(4x-{17}^{∘})+(3x+{3}^{∘})+{60}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 8x+{136}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 8x & ={224}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={28}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500305 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b111120-41dd-5a58-bcc5-b0b6fc78b384" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Sides of a Polygon Given the Sum of Its Interior Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ab977e1-87f4-5761-86af-f2fe440d0bfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499712} {:answer/id #uuid "47613396-5fe7-586c-bc66-d0105e8e4f49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499788} {:answer/id #uuid "542b3dea-7943-560d-ad8d-d052f329538e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499817} {:answer/id #uuid "8696ad5f-9f95-570c-9894-0b78bfff2ece" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499916} {:answer/id #uuid "cbe7ea46-ddc5-572a-81b6-c5feb2fff757" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbe7ea46-ddc5-572a-81b6-c5feb2fff757" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500069} :answer-field/id #uuid "6767309d-2860-5c8c-9e6e-30cf9071e907" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500223}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4852498b-dc1b-525e-82e2-305f7ebaf1ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-23002" :question/problem "The sum of the interior angles of a polygon is ${2700}^{∘}.$ How many sides does it have?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the sum of the interior angles of a polygon with $n$ sides is ${180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2).$\n\nTo find the number of sides in our polygon, we start by setting up the following equation:\n\n$$\n{180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2)=2\\,{700}^{∘}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $n,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2) & =2\\,{700}^{∘} \\\\ n-2 & =\\frac{2\\,{700}^{∘}}{{180}^{∘}} \\\\ n-2 & =15 \\\\ n & =17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the polygon has $n=17$ sides."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500330 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105718 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bad93a16-17d4-50ff-89c8-f3d966df5f1a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unknown Quantities in Quadrilaterals and Pentagons"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50a09afb-1a3c-51a0-85da-c404d79a9d7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{150}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499808} {:answer/id #uuid "53e7832a-ea74-5c30-8ca2-fc9454520d6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{205}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499815} {:answer/id #uuid "78dc7f20-458e-59be-adc9-3e8c6383f239" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{135}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499878} {:answer/id #uuid "a1f780f9-2d19-552a-81f5-1f0f523ddd83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{170}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499969} {:answer/id #uuid "cddf5b4d-4b52-50b1-a7aa-a6060fdc403f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{130}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50a09afb-1a3c-51a0-85da-c404d79a9d7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{150}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499808} :answer-field/id #uuid "21cbe6a6-724d-5863-82b3-b2dda90eaa9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500195}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "97be54c9-28e3-5dbb-97cf-64bffd902d5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-4304" :question/problem "![](images/60/606a6eb139d8e5813f85c608824d8313a97ddaa465b7c05c89173247550a77ee.png)\n\nIn the quadrilateral $ABCD$ shown above, determine the measure of $∠C.$" :question/worked-solution "A quadrilateral has $n=4$ sides. Therefore, the sum of the interior angles of a quadrilateral  must be \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2) & ={180}^{∘}\\cdot (4-2) \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding up the internal angles and solving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A+m∠B+m∠C+m∠D & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ (x+{30}^{∘})+{75}^{∘}+5x+(3x-{15}^{∘}) & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 9x+{90}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 9x & ={270}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠C & =5x \\\\  & =5({30}^{∘}) \\\\  & ={150}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{